1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,260
Why are some USB ports blue?

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:04,133
It's not just decoration.

3
00:00:04,883 --> 00:00:09,083
Blue usually marks USB 3, also called SuperSpeed.

4
00:00:09,363 --> 00:00:13,251
The first version of it runs at up to 5 gigabits per second.

5
00:00:14,001 --> 00:00:17,434
The black ports beside it are usually USB 2.

6
00:00:17,714 --> 00:00:22,919
That tops out at 480 megabits per second, roughly 10 times slower.

7
00:00:23,669 --> 00:00:26,255
But the color is a convention, not a rule.

8
00:00:26,535 --> 00:00:30,338
Some makers use red, teal, or plain black for fast ports.

9
00:00:30,618 --> 00:00:35,040
The SS logo next to the port, or your manual, is the better clue.

10
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:40,942
So plug your fast flash drive or external SSD into the faster port.

11
00:00:41,222 --> 00:00:43,087
Big copies finish much sooner.

12
00:00:43,837 --> 00:00:46,402
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

